        "original_id": "69eb5ab6-d05a-56c8-a91e-5685ef94097e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Lightfoot, Ayisha Davies, Rupert Glasson, Ivan Milat, Bradley Murdoch\n- Films: Wolf Creek, Rogue, Coffin Rock, Bloody Sweet Hit\n- Topics: horror films, Australian thriller films, marketing claims, true-crime inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1990s, the real-life murders of tourists by Ivan Milat later became one of the real-world cases that Wolf Creek resembled.\n- In 2001, the real-life crimes of Bradley Murdoch later became another case that Wolf Creek resembled.\n- Wolf Creek was ambiguously marketed as being based on true events.\n- David Lightfoot worked on the horror films Wolf Creek and Rogue.\n- Bloody Sweet Hit was released in 2007, and Ayisha Davies was a producer of the film.\n- Coffin Rock is an Australian melodramatic thriller film directed by Rupert Glasson and produced by David Lightfoot.\n- Coffin Rock was released in 2009, and Ayisha Davies was a producer of the film.",
